# R3F / WebGL

Use only if the work is spatial. One canvas, not a 3D theme. Load `r3f-best-practices`.

- Never `setState` inside `useFrame`. Mutate refs. Use `delta`.
- No per-frame allocations (`new Vector3()`). Reuse vectors.
- Zustand selectors or `getState()` in `useFrame` — never the whole store.
- Cap `dpr={[1, 2]}`. Compressed GLB/KTX2. Dispose geometries/materials.
- `useGLTF.preload`. Suspense fallback. Toggle `visible`, do not remount.
- Canvas behind DOM; pointer events only where interaction is real.
- Skip or replace with a still on mobile / reduced motion / low GPU.
- Do not use `OrbitControls` as the portfolio camera unless orbit is the point.
- Sync scroll to the scene via Lenis progress or ScrollTrigger `onUpdate`, not CSS scroll on the canvas.